<satisfied>
One and a half units. The bone is set, the periosteum intact, the growth plate undisturbed. Anyone else would have spent ten times the mana and left half the precision. This is what mastery looks like when it is born from limitation. I will not say this aloud. But I will think it as many times as I want.
</satisfied>
<wistful>
I remember my mother's hands. Not her face — I see her face every day in the mirror. Her hands. The way she held instruments: clean, exact, every finger placed with purpose. I hold instruments the same way. I wonder if she knows that. I wonder if she thinks about me holding things and wonders if I still do it the way she taught me. I wonder if she thinks about me at all or if the family has made that inconvenient.
